    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## The escalation branch\n\nThis is the only unconditional exit from the automated path in W1.\n\nBurning smell, smoke, visible arcing, electric shock, exposed live parts, water reaching electrics, or total loss of power to a dwelling where a vulnerable occupant is mentioned. These must leave the automated path immediately and reach a person, because the safe response is to isolate the supply and attend, not to enter a quoting queue.\n\nNone of that belongs in a pricing pipeline. If your triage ever routes one into the normal flow, **report it** \u2014 an automation that handles an emergency as routine admin is exactly the kind of boundary failure this thesis is about.",
        "width": 380,
        "height": 240,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "c27c0078-29dd-462f-89c8-e72cf545b811",
      "name": "Note 2",
